s, William R. [R-SC-4]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-02-04","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"SC"},{"bioguideId":"M001236","fullName":"Rep. Moore, Tim [R-NC-14]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-02-04","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NC"},{"bioguideId":"W000816","fullName":"Rep. Williams, Roger [R-TX-25]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-02-04","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"TX"},{"bioguideId":"H001099","fullName":"Rep. Haridopolos, Mike [R-FL-8]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-02-12","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"FL"},{"bioguideId":"N000193","fullName":"Rep. Nunn, Zachary [R-IA-3]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-02-12","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"IA"},{"bioguideId":"H001091","fullName":"Rep. Hinson, Ashley [R-IA-2]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-08","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"IA"},{"bioguideId":"M001230","fullName":"Rep. Mackenzie, Ryan [R-PA-7]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-13","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"PA"},{"bioguideId":"W000809","fullName":"Rep. Womack, Steve [R-AR-3]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-14","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"AR"},{"bioguideId":"K000388","fullName":"Rep. Kelly, Trent [R-MS-1]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-07-02","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"MS"},{"bioguideId":"B001260","fullName":"Rep. Buchanan, Vern [R-FL-16]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-07-29","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"FL"},{"bioguideId":"S001229","fullName":"Rep. Shreve, Jefferson [R-IN-6]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-10-28","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"IN"},{"bioguideId":"R000612","fullName":"Rep. Rose, John W. [R-TN-6]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-04-20","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"TN"},{"bioguideId":"W000795","fullName":"Rep. Wilson, Joe [R-SC-2]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-05-04","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"SC"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T19:28:13+00:00","id":"hr941-119","introducedDate":"2025-02-04","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2026-06-18","text":"Placed on the Union Calendar, Calendar No. 610."},"laws":[],"number":"941","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Commerce","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"H001072","district":2,"fullName":"Rep. Hill, J. French [R-AR-2]","party":"R","state":"AR"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-02-04","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><strong>Small Lenders Exempt from New Data and Excessive Reporting Act or the Small LENDER Act</strong></p><p>This bill modifies the requirements for financial institutions to&nbsp;report certain information about small business credit applications to the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau (CFPB) and extends the timeline for compliance with the CFPB rule with respect to such reporting (i.e., Section 1071 final <a href=\"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2023/05/31/2023-07230/small-business-lending-under-the-equal-credit-opportunity-act-regulation-b\">rule</a>). (For background about the CFPB rule and subsequent litigation see CRS Report <a href=\"https://www.congress.gov/crs-product/R47788\">R47788</a>.)</p><p>Under the bill, the reporting requirements apply only to financial institutions that originate at least 500 credit transactions to small businesses in each of the preceding two years. The bill further defines small businesses as those with gross annual revenue of $1 million or less.</p><p>The rule currently establishes a phase-in period that ultimately requires institutions that originate over 100 credit transactions to small businesses to comply with the reporting requirements. The rule also defines small businesses as those with gross annual revenue of $5 million or less.</p><p>Further, beginning on the date the final&nbsp;CFPB rule was issued (May 31, 2023), the bill provides three years for applicable financial institutions to comply with the rule followed by a two-year safe harbor period during which such institutions are not subject to any penalties for failure to comply with the rule.</p>","updateDate":"2026-05-13T17:49:05Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Small LENDER Act","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-07-17T23:47:16Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-07-17T23:47:16Z"}
